The portable host implementation was adapted for the Windows port in 2026.
It contains no Linux kernel calls, firmware binary, calibration data or keys.

The escan v1 command and v109 BSS handling follow the same Switchroot brcmfmac
cfg80211.c and brcmutil/d11.c sources, Copyright (c) 2010–2014 Broadcom Corporation.

Broadcom TXPOST encryption exemption and RX completion flags:
  https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/bcmdhd-3.10/drivers/net/wireless/bcmdhd/include/bcmmsgbuf.h
Switchroot infrastructure join and CCMP key format:
  https://github.com/CTCaer/switch-l4t-kernel-4.9/blob/linux-5.1.2/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
Broadcom fixed association-frame headers:
